cuffell@spot.Colorado.EDU writes:
>
>Now a question of my own -- do people really find cockatrices to be
>problem? 

They're about the 4th or 5th thing I genocide.  It's really frustrating
to have cockatrice re-stone you while you're eating a lizard or praying
to try to save yourself from the first stoning attempt.

>As for genociding, the things I take out are generally nymphs, nurses,
>xans, and umber hulks.

These things don't bother me at all:

nymphs: a wand of cancellation or missle weapons (darts, etc.) can take
        care of these easily.
nurses: I'm usually at a high-enough level that they don't really hurt me,
        and it bores me to try to gain HP with them.  (So I don't waste
        either a normal genocide or reverse genocide on them.)
xans: I usually have boots by the time I see them.
umber hulks:  They're great for removing walls in Hell, and for confusing you.
              (For scroll reading.)  I usually have a blindfold by the time
              I get umber hulks, so they only confuse me when I want.

The monsters I hate:

rust monsters: they usually get to me before I've rustproofed my helm, 
               gauntlets, and boots.  (I usually have a unicorn horn by
               the time I see them, though.)
ochre jellies: They do more damage than you think!
liches:        It's very rare, but also very frustrating to have your
               stuff cursed or disintegrated.

and, in hell, gelatenous cubes.  I *hate* it when they team up with minotaurs.

